WM Keyboard data

This repository redistributes, in modified form, the word lists of AOSP
LatinIME (platform/packages/inputmethods/LatinIME, dictionaries/):

  Copyright (C) The Android Open Source Project
  Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0; see
  data/LICENSE-AOSP-APACHE-2.0.txt.

They are the data/*/*_aosp.txt.gz files. scripts/import_aosp.py generates
them and describes what was changed.

It also redistributes the word list of desktop Avro Phonetic (ibus-avro,
avrodict.js) as data/bn/bn_avro_dictionary.txt.gz:

  Copyright (C) OmicronLab
  Licensed under the Mozilla Public License 1.1; see
  data/LICENSE-AVRO-MPL-1.1.txt. Only the encoding changed; data/README.md
  says how.

The offline dictionaries under dictionary/ are derived works of:

  Open English WordNet 2024, https://en-word.net/
  Licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International
  licence (CC BY 4.0). dictionary/en/oewn.wmdict.gz keeps its single-word
  lemmas, definitions, first examples, synonyms, antonyms and
  pronunciations, re-encoded by scripts/build_dictionary_packs.py.

  English Wiktionary, https://en.wiktionary.org/, as extracted by
  kaikki.org (wiktextract). Licensed under CC BY-SA 4.0 and the GNU Free
  Documentation License. dictionary/en/wiktionary.wmdict.gz is a cut of
  it (common single words, a few senses each, shortened examples) and is
  distributed under the same terms.

The word bigram and trigram lists built or improved from Tatoeba
(data/*/*_bigrams.txt.gz, data/*/*_trigrams.txt.gz, generated by
scripts/import_tatoeba_ngrams.py) and the word lists counted from it
(the languages data/README.md lists under "Tatoeba Word Lists", generated by
scripts/import_tatoeba_words.py) are derived works of:

  Tatoeba sentence corpus, https://tatoeba.org/
  Licensed under Creative Commons Attribution 2.0 France (CC BY 2.0 FR)
  and CC0; contributed by the Tatoeba community.

